    "context": {
      "explanation": "Election ticks campaign only for eligible nodes with no committed-but-unapplied entries. Available votes and up-to-date logs qualify support; known-peer response filtering and term dispatch precede aggregation. Higher terms, lost quorum and self-removal can remove authority; transfer waits for a full member to catch up and has a timeout. Reset discards pending read support and remote progress but preserves log commitment. New leadership appends a no-op and reconstructs pending config state. Membership changes are applied by the RSM then reflected in Raft under raftMu; recovery reconstructs snapshot membership and saved term/vote/log before later formation.",
      "behavior_ids": [
        "B-authority",
