    "connection": {
      "explanation": "Support is owned by the current term and installed membership. Authority transitions clear volatile votes/read support/progress, while persisted term/vote and protected committed history constrain future elections and replication. Applied membership updates redefine eligible participants and quorum; election blocking prevents campaigning before committed history is consumed. Confirmed reads bridge leadership support and client consumption through request context and application position, so release and notification are separate responsibilities. Stale-term replies are rejected; forwarded pending requests have distinct context, drop/timeout handling and no implicit completion guarantee from role acquisition.",
